1
00:00:00,195 --> 00:00:02,947
2.3 million gallons of molasses sat

2
00:00:02,947 --> 00:00:04,200
in one steel tank in

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,125
Boston, January 1919.

4
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:08,744
The day before,

5
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:09,848
the air had warmed from

6
00:00:09,848 --> 00:00:11,647
2 to 41 degrees,

7
00:00:11,647 --> 00:00:12,588
and a fresh load of

8
00:00:12,588 --> 00:00:14,171
warm molasses went in.

9
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,793
Just after noon,

10
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,930
the tank burst.

11
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:18,127
Its rivets shot out with

12
00:00:18,127 --> 00:00:19,694
a sound like a machine gun.

13
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,039
A wave 25 feet high

14
00:00:22,039 --> 00:00:23,281
swept through the North End

15
00:00:23,281 --> 00:00:25,254
at 35 miles an hour.

16
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:26,942
As it cooled,

17
00:00:26,942 --> 00:00:28,289
it thickened and trapped those

18
00:00:28,289 --> 00:00:29,031
